            <ArticleTitle>[Slow flow in the coronary system and ST elevation in the ECG in left atrium catheterization].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>789-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A complication of transseptal left atrial catheterization is a transient ST-elevation in the ECG with unknown cause. In this case simultaneous angiography showed a so-called &quot;slow flow&quot; of dye dilution in the coronary artery. A coronary spasm or an embolic occlusion of the coronary artery could be excluded. The reason for this phenomenon might be a reflex increase of the arteriolar resistance with transient ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
